		{
			"id": "threads-vs-actors-title",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 650,
			"y": 230,
			"width": 120,
			"height": 14.95,
			"text": "Threads vs Actors",
			"fontSize": 13,
			"fontFamily": 2,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"roughness": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#FFA500",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"opacity": 100,
			"angle": 0,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"roundness": null,
			"boundElements": [],
			"locked": false,
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Threads vs Actors",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.15,
			"version": 1,
			"versionNonce": 1,
			"index": "b02",
			"isDeleted": false,
			"seed": 1,
			"updated": 1771439400000,
			"link": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": "",
			"verticalAlign": "top"
		},
		{
			"id": "threads-vs-actors-text",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 650,
			"y": 250,
			"width": 260,
			"height": 138,
			"text": "THREADS: OS-level execution units that\nrun code in parallel. Can crash if they\naccess shared data simultaneously.\n\nACTORS: NOT threads! A data protection\nabstraction. Multiple threads CAN call an\nactor at once via 'await'. The actor\nserializes access internally—only one\nexecutes at a time, others SUSPEND\n(not block). Swift runtime manages this.",
			"fontSize": 11,
			"fontFamily": 2,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"roughness": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"opacity": 100,
			"angle": 0,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"roundness": null,
			"boundElements": [],
			"locked": false,
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "THREADS: OS-level execution units that\nrun code in parallel. Can crash if they\naccess shared data simultaneously.\n\nACTORS: NOT threads! A data protection\nabstraction. Multiple threads CAN call an\nactor at once via 'await'. The actor\nserializes access internally—only one\nexecutes at a time, others SUSPEND\n(not block). Swift runtime manages this.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.15,
			"version": 1,
			"versionNonce": 1,
			"index": "b03",
			"isDeleted": false,
			"seed": 1,
			"updated": 1771439400000,
			"link": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
